in China</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2005</year><volume>366</volume><fpage>1821</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16298221</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(05)67344-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blumenthal</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsiao</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Privatisation and its discontents &#x02013; the evolving Chinese health care system</article-title><source>NEJM</source><year>2005</year><volume>353</volume><fpage>1165</fpage><lpage>1170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16162889</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJMhpr051133</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Seeborg</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Jin</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The new rural-to-urban mobility in China: causes and implications</article-title><source>J Socio Econ</source><year>2000</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1053-5357(00)00052-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>ZX</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The population problem in urban economic reform</article-title><source>Population Periodicals</source><year>1995</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>4</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Niauru</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Shadel</surname><given-names>WG</given-names></name><name><surname>Britt</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Abrams</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Response to social stress, urge to smoke and smoking cessation</article-title><source>Addict Behaviour</source><year>2002</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>241</fpage><lpage>250</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0306-4603(00)00180-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Zhejiang Provincial Statistics Bureau</collab></person-group><source>Zhejiang Statistical Year Book 2001</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Hangzhou Zhejiang People's Publisher</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Treiman</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The household registration system and social stratification in China</article-title><year>1955</year><volume>1004;41</volume><fpage>363</fpage><lpage>84</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Chinese Academy of Preventive Medicine</collab></person-group><source>Smoking and health in China: 1996 national survey of smoking patterns</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Beijing: China Science and Technology Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Doll</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Peto</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Boreham</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutherland</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mortality in relation to smoking: 50 years' observations on male British doctors</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2004